<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;ALEXANDRA CARTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alexandra Carter is a renowned Canadian neurologist known for her groundbreaking research in neuroscience, with a focus on neural mechanisms underlying cognitive development and neurological disorders."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0387</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TORONTO, ONTARIO, CANADA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Toronto, Ontario, Canada is the birthplace of Alexandra Carter, where she developed an interest in neuroscience and pursued her undergraduate degree in biology."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0387</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNIVERSITY OF TORONTO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The University of Toronto is where Alexandra Carter earned her undergraduate degree in biology, graduating magna cum laude in 1997."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0387</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FREE UNIVERSITY OF AMSTERDAM (VRIJE UNIVERSITEIT AMSTERDAM)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Free University of Amsterdam is where Alexandra Carter earned her Master's degree in Neuroscience in 2000, heavily influenced by the works of Dutch neuroscientist, Dr. Henk J. Groenewegen."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0387</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNIVERSITY OF BRITISH COLUMBIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The University of British Columbia is where Alexandra Carter completed her Ph.D. research under the supervision of Dr. Timothy H. Murphy, focusing on 'Neural Plasticity and Cognitive Development' and publishing her dissertation in 2005."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0387</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DR. TIMOTHY H. MURPHY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dr. Timothy H. Murphy supervised Alexandra Carter's Ph.D. research at the University of British Columbia, focusing on neural plasticity and cognitive development."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0387</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DR. HENK J. GROENEWEGEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dr. Henk J. Groenewegen influenced Alexandra Carter's work at the Free University of Amsterdam, contributing to her interest in neuroscience."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0387</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNIVERSITY OF MIAMI HOSPITAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"University of Miami Hospital is known for its commitment to innovation and excellence, providing opportunities for research and collaboration."&lt;SEP&gt;"University of Miami Hospital is where Alexandra Carter completed her residency, earning recognition as a leading authority in her field."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0387</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DR. MARIA RODRIGUEZ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dr. Maria Rodriguez was a mentor to Alexandra Carter during her residency at the University of Miami Hospital, specializing in stroke rehabilitation and providing guidance in neuroimaging and neurophysiology."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0387</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNIVERSITY OF MIAMI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"University of Miami is the city where the University of Miami Hospital is located, serving as a crucible for Alexandra Carter's growth and a testing ground for her skills."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0387</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JOURNAL OF NEUROSCIENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Journal of Neuroscience is where Alexandra Carter has published numerous papers, including her dissertation on 'Neural Plasticity and Cognitive Development'."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0387</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NATURE NEUROSCIENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nature Neuroscience is another esteemed scientific journal where Alexandra Carter has published papers, such as 'Neural Mechanisms of Cognitive Development in Children' in 2012."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0387</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANADIAN INSTITUTES OF HEALTH RESEARCH (CIHR) YOUNG INVESTIGATOR AWARD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The CIHR Young Investigator Award is an award Alexandra Carter received for her contributions to the field of neuroscience in 2010."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0387</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NATIONAL SCIENCE FOUNDATION (NSF) CAREER AWARD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The NSF CAREER Award is another prestigious award Alexandra Carter received in 2015 for her research in neuroscience."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0387</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEUROSCIENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Neuroscience is the field of study that Alexandra Carter specializes in, focusing on the neural mechanisms underlying cognitive development and neurological disorders."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0387</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEURAL PLASTICITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Neural Plasticity is a key concept in Alexandra Carter's research, referring to the brain's ability to change and adapt over time."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0387</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COGNITIVE DEVELOPMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cognitive Development is a central theme in Alexandra Carter's research, exploring how the brain develops and changes throughout life."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0387</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEUROLOGICAL DISORDERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Neurological Disorders are a focus area in Alexandra Carter's research, investigating the neural mechanisms underlying various disorders."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0387</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STROKE REHABILITATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stroke Rehabilitation is a specialized area of expertise for Dr. Maria Rodriguez, a mentor to Alexandra Carter."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0387</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEUROIMAGING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Neuroimaging is a technique used by Dr. Maria Rodriguez to study the brain, which Alexandra Carter was exposed to during her residency."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0387</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DR. CARTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dr. Carter is recognized as a leading authority in her field after extensive work at the University of Miami Hospital involving observation, collaboration, and experimentation."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0387</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OBSERVATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Observation refers to the process of watching and recording data at the University of Miami Hospital."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0387</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLLABORATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Collaboration involves working together with others at the University of Miami Hospital to achieve research goals."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0387</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXPERIMENTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Experimentation is the process of conducting tests and trials at the University of Miami Hospital to advance knowledge."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0387</data>
    </node>
